I "hacked" up a perl script that plays randomly selected nethack
characters.  It allows you to specify a mix of characters you like
to play along with a distribution, so you can play 30% wizards, 10%
cavemen, 35% valkyries and 25% healers, if you like.

The documentation is in the comment.  Enjoy!  Please send comments to me.

#! /usr/local/bin/perl
#  !!! Change the above path to wherever you put perl. !!!
#  Written by Matthew Merzbacher (matthew@cs.ucla.edu)
#  1993 - permission to redistribute for free

# usage:
#
# nh
#    play nethack with random character selected from default list
#
# nh -args
#    calls nethack with arguments as normal.
#    Example: nh -s all
#
# nh chars
#    play nethack, randomly selecting character from "chars".
#    Example: nh vvvww
#      This plays only wizards and valkyries, with a 60% chance of
#      getting a valkyrie.
#    args is case insensitive (here, and below)
#
# nh +chars
#    play nethack with random selection from default list, plus chars.
#    Example: nh +www
#      This plays some random character, but you're more likely to get
#      a wizard (4/16).
#
# nh ^chars
#    play nethack with random selection from default list, minus chars.
#    Example: nh ^epr
#      This plays some random character, but no elves, priests or rogues.
#    Example: nh ^a-t
#      This plays only valkyries and wizards (equivalent to: nh wv)
#
# nh ^chars1 +chars2
#    you can combine the two to both add and subtract chars
#    Example: nh ^e-t +wwwhh
#      play a random character, with emphasis on wizards and healers, but
#      no elves, knights, priests, rogues, samurai or tourists.
#      note that healers were deleted (by ^e-t) and then readded.  The
#      list of chars is then: ABCVWWWWHH

$chars="ABCEHKPRSTVW";

$remove="";
$add="";

while ($#ARGV >= 0) {
  if (@ARGV[0] =~ /^-/) { exec ("nethack",@ARGV); }
  elsif (@ARGV[0] =~ /^\^/) { $remove = @ARGV[0]; $remove =~ s/\^//; }
  elsif (@ARGV[0] =~ /^\+/) { $add = @ARGV[0]; $add =~ s/\+//; }
  elsif (@ARGV[0] =~ /^[A-Za-z]/) { $chars = @ARGV[0]; }
  elsif (@ARGV[0] =~ /^\?/) {
    print "usage: nh [-args] [+chars] [^chars] [chars]\n";
    print "with no arguments, randomly selects a character\n";
    print "\t-args\tcalls nethack with args\n";
    print "\t+chars\tadd chars to random mix\n";
    print "\t^chars\tremoves chars from random mix\n";
    print "\tchars\tuses chars for random mix\n";
    exit;
    }
  else { die "Can't parse argument: @ARGV[0]"; }
  shift;
  }

$chars =~ y/a-z/A-Z/;
$remove =~ y/a-z/A-Z/;
$add =~ y/a-z/A-Z/;

$chars =~ s/[$remove]//g if ($remove);
$chars .= $add if ($add);

srand(time);

exec ("nethack -".substr($chars,int(rand(length($chars))),1));


